Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  SARAH P THAYER  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right breast re excision for invasive ductal carcinoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  MULTIFOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  EXTENDING TO THE SUPERIOR MARGIN AND  0 1 CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  WITH A SEVERELY ATYPICAL FOCUS  0 1 CM FROM THE INFERIOR MARGIN  3  FIBROADENOMA  4  PROLIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunostains for p63  SM MHC  calponin  and cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 do not reveal evidence of invasive carcinoma  Results of a cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE immunostain support a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast tissue   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of gray pink to tan yellow fibrofatty tissue partially surfaced along the superficial aspect by an REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan pink skin ellipse  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar which comes to 0 1cm of the medial skin margin  A short black stitch designates the superior margin and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior margin is inked black  the superior margin is inked green and the inferior margin is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a fairly well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated gray white nodule with eccentric focal hemorrhage  The nodule abuts the posterior margin and comes to 0 5cm of the superior margin  1 5cm of the inferior margin  and greater than 2 0cm from all additional margins  0 7cm from this nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm cavity consistent with the previous biopsy site which comes to 0 4cm of the superior margin  0 6cm of the inferior margin  0 5cm of the posterior margin  and greater than 0 2cm from all additional margins  Surrounding the cavity is focally indurated dense gray white fibrous tissue with a poorly delineated indurated area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm that abuts the posterior margin  This area comes to 0 3cm of the inferior margin  0 9cm of the superior margin  and greater than 2 0cm from all additional margins  Also noted surrounding the cavity is chalky yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis and focal hemorrhage  Finally  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm gray white to tan yellow nodule medially which comes to 0 6cm of the posterior margin  0 7cm of the superior margin  1 6cm of the inferior margin  and greater than 2 0cm from all additional margins  This nodule is also 1 4cm medial to the first described nodule  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the medial end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the lateral end margin radially sectioned as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the medial most nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the first described nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the second described indurated area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and midline cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   Breast  Right   Re excision  report_end  , Absent.
