Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Jill Ono  M D  Signed Out by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma  and ADH  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  MASS OF NECROTIC DEBRIS  WITH FIBROSIS  FOCAL CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND  A PLASMA CELL AND HISTIOCYTIC REACTION CONSISTENT WITH NECROTIC TUMOR  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  FOCALLY INVOLVING A PAPILLOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT ADJACENT TO A HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL   AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  FOCAL  4 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  ALL  SEVEN  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF TUMOR  NOTE  No viable invasive tumor is seen  Necrotic tissue is present at the lateral anterior margin along a broad front  The margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN TWENTY ONE LYMPH NODES  0 21   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  and REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm left mastectomy with a suture marking the axillary region of the specimen  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm ellipse of skin is unremarkable and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue and posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm yellow tan  well circumscribed mass in the axillary region  0 2cm from the posterior margin  and 0 5cm from the anterior margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan fibrous area  just superior to the nipple where a metal clip is identified  This area is 0 9cm from the anterior margin and 3 7cm from the posterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and lobulated to focally tan and fibrous  An intraparenchymal lymph node is identified in the lower outer quadrant breast tissue  The axillary region is dissected for lymph nodes and several candidate lymph nodes are grossly identified  There is one candidate lymph node that grossly abuts the axillary mass  Sections are submitted as follows  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  submitted from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant breast parenchyma to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin from lateral portion of skin ellipse   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two additional candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single large lymph node in axillary region which appears to abut the axillary mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intraparenchymal lymph node  bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of yellow lobulated soft tissue that is dissected for lymph nodes  Several candidate lymph nodes are identified and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla   Dissection  report_end  , Present.
