f a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy consisting of breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and axillary tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The nipple and areola appear grossly unremarkable  however  on the ellipse of skin approximately 1 0cm inferior to the nipple is a reddish brown area of ecchymosis measuring 3 0cm in greatest dimension  Immediately adjacent to this area of ecchymosis in the adipose tissue is a small well circumscribed  firm yellowish tan lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The lesion extends to approximately 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  In the remaining breast parenchyma there are multiple ill defined  firm  white nodules which are mainly in the superior medial quadrant  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  and twelve probable lymph nodes are identified  ranging in size from 0 5cm to 2 0cm  SECTION CODE  A  representative sections of overlying skin B D  representative sections of the lesion and deepest resection margin E H  contain representative sections of the nodular areas superior I  contains representative sections of five possible lymph nodes J  contains representative sections of three possible lymph nodes K  contains representative sections of three possible lymph nodes L  contains representative section from one possible lymph node  Submitted separately  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  level  1 lymph node material  is a single piece of adipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is bisected and serially sectioned to reveal mainly adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are identified  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in M and N  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Absent.
