Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 36 CLINICAL DATA  49 year old woman for an incisional biopsy of a breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE   PRESENT ON 2 OF 3 SLIDES   HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood or lymphatic vascular invasion is identified  Invasion of the stroma is not seen  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 58 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain diffusely for CEA and focally for Leu 7  The tumor cells do not stain for chromogranin  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma in not present in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  are two fibrous fragments of breast tissue  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue as well as a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lobulated tan white mass present at the inked margin  Specimen submitted in its entirety in cassettes A through C  with the nodular area in A  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  1  LEFT BREAST   NO LESIONS GROSSLY DEFINITIVE FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Present.
