Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Severe atypical ductal hyperplasia on core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1 OF 3  ISOLATED FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  IN THE REGION OF THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE    REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERO LATERAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCALLY ASSOCIATED WITH LUMINAL MUCIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the pertinent focus and concurs with the diagnosis of focal ductal carcinoma in situ  Multiple levels were examined for the purpose of diagnosis  There is insufficient tissue to perform hormone receptor studies  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy specimen  The short suture indicating anterior  long indicating lateral and bowtie indication cephalad  This specimen has a guide wire in place entering at the medial aspect  The anterior is inked blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined tan solid nodule in the superior aspect of the specimen focally abutting anterior  posterior  and superior aspect  The cut surface of the nodule is 0 6cm in diameter  The specimen also contains small areas of hemorrhage  The specimen is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   including the medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the sections of the nodule in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 47 CLINICAL DATA  Suspicious left breast mass  Suspicious FNA at MGH REMOVED_DATE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of tan soft tissue  submitted in toto to Cassette A  Gross Description by  DANIEL ALMGREN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
